# Private-repo material that has no business in a PUBLIC repo, ignored as a
# SECOND line rather than as the only one. The private-name class in
# scripts/public-repo-guard.sh is the first, and it depends on an operator's
# list existing and being armed; this does not depend on anything. Neither
# replaces the other — a file whose name carries no customer name still belongs
# only in the private repo, and a guard that is skipped ("no pattern
# configured") still leaves this standing.
#
# ONE line, not two. A pattern with no leading slash matches at ANY depth, so
# this covers `businessplan-2026/` and `docs/internal/businessplan-2026/` alike —
# measured with `git check-ignore -v`, which attributes both paths to this line.
# The anchored twin was written first and dropped: git never consulted it, and a
# rule nothing consults is the kind that rots while looking like coverage.
businessplan-2026/

*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
secrets.json
coverage/
tests/performance/results.json
tests/performance/*.log
scripts/bench-models/results/*
!scripts/bench-models/results/.gitkeep
scripts/set-bench/results/*
!scripts/set-bench/results/.gitkeep
tests/fixtures/voice/*.webm
tests/fixtures/voice/*.wav
tests/fixtures/voice/*.mp3
tests/fixtures/voice/*.ogg
tests/fixtures/voice/*.json
tests/fixtures/voice/*.bin
*.debug.log
.playwright-mcp/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.wrangler/
.claude/settings.local.json
.audits/
audits/

# Real thread content, kept out of a public repo by a mechanism rather than a
# comment. Defence in depth, and it is worth being exact about what it is second
# to: `scripts/knowledge-gold-gen.ts` writes the gold DRAFT and REFUSES to write
# anywhere inside a git repo at all (`assertOutsideGitRepo`, defaulting to
# ~/.lynox/knowledge-gold/). That is the primary control and it is a refusal, not
# a warning. These rules cover what a refusal cannot: a file copied in by hand, an
# editor's autosave, an export dropped in the tree by a script that has no such
# check — none of which survive `git add -A` on their own.
#
# ⚠ An earlier version of this comment credited `scripts/gold-propose-sonnet.mjs`
# with the warnings it said a `git add -A` would defeat. That file has never been
# on main; it exists only on `wip/model-fitness-dk-scripts`, and the justification
# was read out of a branch this repo does not ship. Corrected 2026-09-03 — the
# rules below are unchanged and were always right; only the reason was borrowed.
#
# The gold format is DUAL: `tests/eval/knowledge-substrate-score.ts` loads
# `.jsonl` line-by-line and parses anything else as a `.json` GoldCorpus, and the
# eval header names both as "real thread content [that] must never land in the
# public core repo". So both halves are covered, plus the copies a shell habit
# produces (`cp x.jsonl x.jsonl.bak`).
#
# ⚠️ HONEST LIMIT: this is extension matching, and the `.json` half cannot be
# closed that way — a GoldCorpus named `corpus.json` or `threads.json` passes.
# Closing it properly needs a pre-commit guard that reads STRUCTURE (a `turns[]`
# or `gold[]` array), not a name. Until that exists, the name patterns below are
# defence in depth, not a guarantee.
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.*
*.ndjson
*gold*.json
*gold-set*.json

# The kg-bench corpora are re-allowed. Note what this does and does not do: all
# four are ALREADY TRACKED, and .gitignore never applies to tracked files — so
# these lines do not keep them; they keep FUTURE files in those two directories
# addable. Marker scan over all four (real names, e-mail, phone, IBAN): 0 hits.
# The corpora carry a `fixtureId` on every row; the query catalog does not, and
# is synthetic by reference — it only names fixture ids in `expected_topK_ids`.
#
# ⚠️ `*` does not cross `/`: a file directly in `corpus/` or `queries/` is
# already covered by the lines below and needs nothing. A new SUBDIRECTORY does
# — allow it with its own `!` line and say in the commit why it carries no real
# content. Silence is the safe default: a missing fixture fails a test, a
# committed transcript cannot be taken back.
!scripts/kg-bench/corpus/*.jsonl
!scripts/kg-bench/queries/*.jsonl
